{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>But if there shall be harm</b> to the woman. <b>And you shall give a life for a life.</b> Our Rabbis, of blessed memory, disagreed concerning this. Some of them say: an actual life, for he is a murderer who killed the woman, and even though he did not intend her, he is liable. And others say: monetary compensation — for since he did not intend her but intended to kill this one and killed that one, he is exempt [from capital punishment]." "<b>And in the Midrash</b> of Rabbi Shimon ben Yochai I saw: ״if men strive״ — this is Michael and Samael; ״and they hurt a woman with child״ — this is Kenesset Yisrael; ״and her children come out״ — in exile; ״he shall surely be punished״ — Samael shall be punished, ״as the woman's husband shall lay upon him״ — this is the Holy One, blessed be He, as it is said: ״and he shall give judgment״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:39.785499683Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}